# Cryptocurrency Explorer - Development Rules

Cryptocurrency Explorer - Cursor IDE Execution Guide

Detailed Step-by-Step Implementation Plan

Overview

Pre-Development Setup (10 minutes)

1. Git Repository Setup
main: Production-ready code only
develop: Primary development branch
feature/xxx: Individual features (optional for speed)
Commit frequently with descriptive messages[ 132][^135] 129][

2. Cursor IDE Configuration
## Core Instructions
- Only modify code directly relevant to the specific request
- Never replace code with placeholders like "// ... rest of the code ..."
- Always provide complete, functional code
- Break problems into smaller steps and implement completely
- Use TypeScript with proper typing (basic typing acceptable for speed)
## Project Context
This is a Next.js 14 cryptocurrency assets explorer with:
- Frontend: Next.js 14 App Router, React, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS
- Backend: Next.js API Routes, Supabase database
- External API: CoinGecko public API for crypto data
- Goal: Complete core features in 4 hours maximum
## Code Standards
- Use kebab-case for file names: user-profile.tsx
- Use PascalCase for React components: UserProfile
- Use camelCase for variables and props: userSettings
- Mobile-first responsive design with Tailwind CSS
- Client-side data fetching with proper error handling
## Architecture Patterns
- Component-based architecture with reusable UI components
- API Routes for backend endpoints with proper error handling
- In-memory caching for external API calls (60-second TTL)
- TypeScript interfaces for all data structures
- Proper separation of concerns: components, lib, utils, types
## Commit Strategy
- Make small, specific commits for each feature
- Use conventional commit messages: "feat:", "fix:", "docs:"
- Commit frequently to show development progress
- Test functionality before committing
